Sure! Below is a minimal example of a “flip‑card” that rotates (in 3D) when you hover over it.  
Feel free to copy the code into an `.html` file and open it in your browser.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Hover‑Rotate Card</title>
<style>
/* 1️⃣  Set up the outer wrapper – this gives the 3D space */
.card-wrapper {
    width: 300px;          /* card width */
    height: 200px;         /* card height */
    perspective: 800px;    /* how far the viewer is from the card */
    margin: 50px auto;     /* center horizontally */
}

/* 2️⃣  The card itself – positioned relative so we can absolutely position its sides */
.card {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    position: relative;
    transform-style: preserve-3d;   /* keep children in 3D space */
    transition: transform 0.6s ease; /* smooth animation */
}

/* 3️⃣  When hovering over the wrapper, rotate the card */
.card-wrapper:hover .card {
    transform: rotateY(180deg); /* change to rotateX(180deg) for vertical flip */
}

/* 4️⃣  Front & back faces – both occupy the same space */
.card-face {
    position: absolute;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    backface-visibility: hidden; /* hide the backside when it's turned away */
    border-radius: 10px;
    overflow: hidden;
    box-shadow: 0 4px 8px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
}

/* 5️⃣  Front face styling */
.card-front {
    background: #fff;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    color: #333;
}

/* 6️⃣  Back face styling – rotated 180° so it starts hidden */
.card-back {
    background: #f8f8f8;
    transform: rotateY(180deg); /* start flipped */
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    color: #555;
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card-wrapper">
    <div class="card">
        <div class="card-face card-front">
            Front Side
        </div>
        <div class="card-face card-back">
            Back Side
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Step | What happens | Why |
|------|--------------|-----|
| 1 | `perspective` on `.card-wrapper` | Gives depth to the 3D transform. |
| 2 | `transform-style: preserve-3d` on `.card` | Keeps child elements in 3D space instead of flattening them. |
| 3 | Hover rule on `.card-wrapper:hover .card` | Rotates the whole card when the mouse hovers over the wrapper. |
| 4 | `backface-visibility: hidden` on each face | Hides the side that’s facing away from the viewer. |
| 5 | `.card-back` rotated 180° initially | Places the back face behind the front face at the start. |

#### Customization tips

- **Change the rotation axis**: replace `rotateY(180deg)` with `rotateX(180deg)` for a vertical flip.
- **Adjust speed**: modify `transition: transform 0.6s ease;` to make it faster/slower.
- **Add more content**: put images, text, buttons inside `.card-front` or `.card-back`.
- **Add shadows or gradients**: style the faces as you wish.

That’s all you need to create a simple rotating card with pure CSS!
